From 337141912a3a266acd98a330a5e1cd51d724dae5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AKENO NETWORK <noreply@akeno.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:32:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AKENO direct entry: open one plugin's page from the Toolbox
 shortcut or the game options menu

- OnionHEN?Plugin=<ID> (boot-URI hook) redirects to the Toolbox route like
  OnionHEN?Cheats; the resource hook then serves that plugin's root page as
  the Settings root, once, on a fresh dynamic page stack. Without a
  renderable page the Toolbox root opens as before.
- [shortcuts] toolbox_target=toolbox|<plugin ID>: the existing Toolbox
  shortcut (L2+R3 held, Share, long Share) opens that plugin's page.
- [game_menu] plugin_entry=none|<plugin ID>: one entry next to
  "Check for update" in a game's options menu, opening the same URI.
- x64 relocator: an existing jmp [rip+0]; dq hook patch (a detour of an
  earlier injection) is relocated as one 14-byte unit, so a repeated
  injection chains to the old hook for every layout instead of failing
  "relocation failed at +6" for some builds.

Defaults keep the upstream behaviour; config files stay compatible both ways.
